===============================================================================
THE SHORT VERSION
===============================================================================

This project is free. Use it, learn from it, remix it, build on it — for
yourself, for a friend, for a class project, for a non-profit, for
literally anything that isn't about selling this software itself. The one
thing this license asks for is a little credit, and a promise not to turn
around and sell what was given away for free.

===============================================================================
WHAT YOU CAN DO
===============================================================================

You're welcome to:

  - Use DD Compressor for any personal, educational, non-profit, or other
    non-commercial purpose, with no restrictions.
  - Copy, study, and modify the source code.
  - Redistribute the original or your own modified version, as long as you
    follow the two rules below.
  - Use it inside a larger project of your own — including one you charge
    for — as long as DD Compressor (or a modified version of it) isn't
    itself the product being sold. This tool can be a free ingredient in
    something bigger; it can't become someone else's paid app.

===============================================================================
TWO RULES
===============================================================================

RULE 1 — KEEP THE CREDIT.
Any copy or substantial portion of this software, modified or not, must
keep this notice and clearly credit the original author, linking back to
the original repository:

    Originally created by Darshan Patel
    https://github.com/darshandpatel63-prog/DD-COMPRESSER-PRIVACY-FIRST-COMPRESSER

This can live in your README, an "About" or credits screen, or the source
code itself — it just has to be there, intact, and not buried.

RULE 2 — DON'T SELL IT.
You may not charge money — in INR, USD, or any other currency — for this
software or a modified version of it, whether as a one-time sale, a
"premium" tier, a subscription, or behind any paywall, without the
original author's separate written permission. Free means free for
everyone, indefinitely — not free until someone decides to charge for it.

===============================================================================
IF RULE 2 GETS BROKEN
===============================================================================

Anyone who sells, sublicenses for a fee, or otherwise commercially charges
for this software or a modified version of it, without written permission,
agrees to pay the original author INR 5,00,000 (or the equivalent in USD
or the violator's local currency at the time of the violation) as
compensation, in addition to any other legal remedy available.

(That figure is a starting point, not a legal absolute — see the honest
note at the end of this file. Change it to whatever amount you actually
want if you're the one editing this.)

This clause isn't here to scare off anyone using or sharing the project in
good faith. It exists so "free for everyone" keeps meaning that.

